  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '

    On the morning of January 19, 2008, police discovered a "snowman"
    composed of the partial remains of four female bodies and the severed head of
    another woman in front of a women''s dormitory building. Subsequent identification
    confirmed that the four bodies belonged to students of the university, all residents
    of dormitory room 209. However, the severed head was identified as belonging
    to a young woman from another province who had no prior enrollment record at
    the university. The bodies were deliberately arranged, facing the main entrance
    of the dormitory building. Despite the extreme nature of the crime, it displayed
    a clear internal logic, indicating that it was not a random act of violence but
    rather an act of revenge targeting a specific group. The estimated time of death
    coincided with the beginning of the winter break. Due to the holiday period,
    no witnesses were found, and heavy snowfall completely obscured all footprint
    evidence at the scene.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0d31a543563d72d4885373c401d2d483, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 8071613318806429051, guid: 0d31a543563d72d4885373c401d2d483, type: 2}
